ouble-precision format.However, the format used to implement long double varies by platform. Common choices include:8-byte IEEE 754 double-precision format (same as double).80-bit (often padded to 12 or 16 bytes) x87 extended-precision format (compatible with IEEE 754).16-byte IEEE 754 quadruple-precision format.16-byte double-double format (not compatible with IEEE 754).Floating point variables and literalsHere are some definitions of floating point variables:float f;
double d;
